<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH PHILIP MORRIS UNIT 96 NET PROFIT FALLS.</title>
<headline>CZECH PHILIP MORRIS UNIT 96 NET PROFIT FALLS.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech cigarette maker Tabak a.s., majority owned by Philip Morris Cos Inc, said on Wednesday its net profit dipped to 1.6 billion crowns in 1996 from 1.8 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>The firm said in a statement that gross profit fell to 2.3 billion last year from 1995's 3.1 billion crowns.</p>
</text>
